<title>FRANCE: France to raise 22 bln Ffr in corporate tax.</title>
<headline>France to raise 22 bln Ffr in corporate tax.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>France will raise 22 billion francs from additional corporate taxes, Finance Minister Dominique Strauss-Kahn said on Monday.</p>
<p>He told a news conference that six billion francs would be generated by an increase in capital gains tax and 16 billion from increased tax on profits.</p>
</text>
